# Pipeline tooling (`_work/`)

## Main entry

```bash
node _work/normalize.mjs --topic "Topic Name"
```

Reads `_work/md/{Topic}/`, writes `_work/clean/{Topic}/`. Pick formatter by topic name in `normalize.mjs`:

| Topic match | Formatter |
|-------------|-----------|
| C# | `format-csharp-clean.mjs` |
| Angular | `format-angular-clean.mjs` |
| Javascript | `format-javascript-clean.mjs` |
| TypeScript | `format-typescript-clean.mjs` |
| React | `format-react-clean.mjs` |
| Sql Server | `format-sqlserver-clean.mjs` |
| Microservices | `format-microservices-clean.mjs` |
| Docker / Kubernetes | respective `format-*-clean.mjs` |
| Azure Cloud / DevOps | `format-azurecloud-clean.mjs` / `format-azuredevops-clean.mjs` |
| DSA | `format-dsa-clean.mjs` |
| Git, Bash, Certificates, Testing, Security | `format-generic-clean.mjs` / `format-security-clean.mjs` |

## Other scripts

- `build-study-guide.mjs` — regenerate `_work/STUDY.md`
- `enrich-tight-footers.mjs` — append `## Related Topics` from `topic-manifest.json`
- `audit-all-tight.mjs` — tight vs clean parity across all topics
- `audit-{topic}-tight.mjs` — per-topic audits

## Formatter conventions

- Export `formatFile(raw, fileBaseName)` from `format-*-clean.mjs`
- Reuse existing formatters (e.g. React/TypeScript extend Javascript/Angular) rather than duplicating
- **Never** duplicate `export function formatFile` and `export { formatFile }` in the same file

## Do not

- Run destructive bulk “repair” on tight files without verifying TOC + code blocks
- Use `git checkout` to fix content bugs — edit files surgically
- Add `package.json` or build tooling unless the user requests it
